# Project Configuration Rule

## Config File: config/project.yaml

This file is the **single source of truth** for all project-level settings.
Every agent and rule reads from this file. Never hard-code project-specific values in rules.

## Config Hierarchy

```
config/
├── project.yaml          ← Active project config (auto-updated by discovery)
├── project.template.yaml ← Blank template for new projects
└── examples/
    ├── react-javascript.yaml
    ├── react-typescript.yaml
    ├── node-express-api.yaml
    ├── python-fastapi.yaml
    ├── java-spring-boot.yaml
    └── next-fullstack.yaml
```

## How Agents Use Config

### Reading tech stack
```yaml
# Agents read tech section to determine:
# - What linter to run
# - What test runner to execute
# - What formatter to apply
# - What build tool to use
```

### Overriding defaults
Config values override rule defaults. If `codingStandards.maxFunctionLines: 15`
is set, the development rule uses 15, not the default 10.

### Protected fields
Agents MUST NOT overwrite these fields without user confirmation:
- `project.name`
- `project.description`
- `project.domain`
- `integrations.jira.*`
- `integrations.git.defaultBranch`
- `deployment.*`

### Auto-updatable fields (updated by discovery agent)
- `tech.*` (detected from package.json, build files)
- `project.detectedAt` (timestamp of last scan)
- `codingStandards.conventions` (inferred from existing code patterns)

## Config Validation

Before starting work, validate config:
- [ ] `project.name` is set (not "unknown")
- [ ] `tech.primaryLanguage` is detected
- [ ] `commands.test` resolves to an executable command
- [ ] `commands.lint` resolves to an executable command

If validation fails, report which fields need attention and offer to run discovery.

## Extending Config

To add a new field:
1. Add it to `project.template.yaml` with a comment explaining its purpose
2. Add it to the relevant example config files
3. Update the discovery agent to auto-detect the value where possible
4. Document the new field in `agentic-pdlc-framework/docs/configuration.md`
